From 978ba583d94de9834f6d968f08513e3ec5d931b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:26:25 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] decision: accept images in /v1/systemone

Add an images field to System One requests, base64 like /api/generate. Every
question carries the images on its user message, so prompts render through the
same image tagging as chat (imageTaggedMessages), and the request needs a model
with the vision capability.

The llama-server scorer sends rows with media as multimodal prompts: each
[img-N] tag is replaced by the runner's media marker and must appear exactly
once and in order. Those rows skip the token-id primer (llama-server's prompt
cache still reuses the shared prefix), and usage counts the embedded image
positions llama-server reports.

The 64 KiB cap still applies to the text of the request; base64 images may add
up to 32 MiB.
