 This returns a refund probability of `0.9989` and an urgency score of `0.8308` on the 0–2 scale (rounded). Results can vary with the model and configuration.
 
+## Ask about images
+
+A decision model with the vision capability can answer questions about images. Pass them as base64 strings in `images`, as with `/api/generate`; every question sees all of them, along with the state:
+
+```shell images.sh
+curl http://localhost:11434/v1/systemone \
+  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
+  -d '{
+    "model": "my-vision-decision-model",
+    "state": {"note": "The customer says the parcel arrived damaged."},
+    "images": ["'"$(base64 -w0 parcel.jpg)"'"],
+    "questions": {
+      "damaged": {"type": "noul", "instructions": "Does the parcel in the photo look damaged?"}
+    }
+  }'
+```
+
+A model without the vision capability returns 400 for a request with images. The model must be trained to answer System One prompts with images, with the image tags placed where its template puts them.
+
 See the [API reference](/api/systemone) for request fields, limits, errors, and token usage.
